\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12.3}{\ignorespaces \emph  {Radon-domain sliced barycentric interpolation between the cat and heart densities.} The columns correspond to $t=0,0.2,\ldots  ,1$. The first row shows the endpoint densities and the intermediate reconstructions $A_t$ defined in\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq-radon-display-reconstruction}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}} from the windowed pseudoinverse\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq-radon-windowed-ramp}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}. The second row shows the projected-density fields $h_t$ (labeled $R_t$ in the figure), obtained by converting the directionwise quantile barycenters back into one-dimensional densities. The third row shows the quantile fields $Q_t$ defined in\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq-radon-barycenter-quantile-field}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}. This illustrates both the simplicity of one-dimensional quantile interpolation and the extra pseudoinverse reconstruction step needed to return from Radon data to an image density.}}{246}{figure.12.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sliced-radon-barycenter}{{12.3}{246}{\emph {Radon-domain sliced barycentric interpolation between the cat and heart densities.} The columns correspond to $t=0,0.2,\ldots ,1$. The first row shows the endpoint densities and the intermediate reconstructions $A_t$ defined in~\eqref {eq-radon-display-reconstruction} from the windowed pseudoinverse~\eqref {eq-radon-windowed-ramp}. The second row shows the projected-density fields $h_t$ (labeled $R_t$ in the figure), obtained by converting the directionwise quantile barycenters back into one-dimensional densities. The third row shows the quantile fields $Q_t$ defined in~\eqref {eq-radon-barycenter-quantile-field}. This illustrates both the simplicity of one-dimensional quantile interpolation and the extra pseudoinverse reconstruction step needed to return from Radon data to an image density}{figure.12.3}{}}
