\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.4}{\ignorespaces \emph  {Discrete Wasserstein distances on small Markov-chain simplices.} Left: the closed-form profiles \(r\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow \mathcal  W_K(a_r,a_{r_0})\), with \(a_r=(r,1-r)\), for several anchors \(r_0\) on \(\Sigma _2\). Middle: numerical level sets of \(\mathcal  W_K(a,\bar  a)\) on \(\Sigma _3\), where \(\bar  a=(1/3,1/3,1/3)\), computed from the local Riemannian norm induced by the complete-neighbor Markov chain. Right: the corresponding level sets for the ordinary \(\Wass  _2\) distance with \(d(i,j)=1\) for \(i\neq j\), i.e.\ \(\Wass  _2^2(a,\bar  a)=|\!| a-\bar  a |\!|_{\mathrm  {TV}}\).}}{330}{figure.14.4}\protected@file@percent }
